DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260904
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-MICROSOFT-MSNCALENDAR-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
SUMMARY:Exhibition: "Hidden Layers: AI Infrastructures and Hallucinations"
LOCATION:Worth Ryder Art Gallery\, Anthropology &amp\; Art Building\, Rm 1
 16
DESCRIPTION:The Department of German and the Department of Art Practice ar
 e excited to announce the opening of Hidden Layers: AI Infrastructures and
  Hallucinations\, curated by Antonio Somaini with Hannes Bajohr and Sonja 
 Thiel\, in dialogue with the France–Berkeley research initiative The Lat
 ent Spaces of Culture\, and on display at the Worth Ryder Art Gallery. Thi
 s exhibition examines some of the concealed dimensions of contemporary AI 
 culture — the planetary infrastructures of extraction and computation\, 
 the often invisible human labor\, the latent vector spaces within which cu
 lture is compressed and processed\, and the models' hallucinations. Hidden
  Layers tackles these phenomena from two different perspectives: AI Infras
 tructures and AI Hallucinations. Featuring works by Nouf Aljowaysir\; Gaš
 per and Nina Beguš & Metahaven\; Grégory Chatonsky\; Kate Crawford & Vla
 dan Joler\; Asma Kazmi & Jill Miller\; Andrea Khôra\; Occitane Lacurie & 
 Barnabé Sauvage\; Greg Niemeyer\; and Mario Santamaria & Alex Saum-Pascua
 l. The project is a collaboration between the Department of German and the
  Worth Ryder Art Gallery at the Department of Art Practice.Exhibition Date
 s: September 3 - October 3\, 2026Opening Reception: Thursday\, September 3
 \, 4-6:30pm\, Worth Ryder Art Gallery RSVP here (https://docs.google.com/f
 orms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd_OOMe7YQHw3CYbSr673UCSlQ0f4mn4lZ7g46KhRUTRpC5qQ/viewform
 ?usp=dialog)Artist Talk\, Gregory Chatonsky: Thursday\, September 3\, 6:30
 -8:00pm\, AAPB 285 RSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd_
 OOMe7YQHw3CYbSr673UCSlQ0f4mn4lZ7g46KhRUTRpC5qQ/viewform?usp=dialog)Related
  programming:Film Program: September 9\, 7 pm\, BAMPFAWorkshop on Latent S
 paces of Culture: September 9\, 2pm-4pm\; September 10/11\, 9:30 am-4pm on
  both days\, 470 Stephens&#160\;Additional events and more details to be a
 nnounced. Times subject to change\, please also check the campus calendar.
  This exhibition is supported by the France-Berkeley Fund of the Institute
  of European Studies\, the Department of German and the Department of Art 
 Practice\, together with the Berkeley Center for New Media\, the Berkeley 
 Institute for Data Science (BIDS)\, Department of Rhetoric\; Antikythera\,
  the Pamela P. Fong and Family Distinguished Chair in China Studies\, the 
 Division of Arts & Humanities\, the Townsend Center for the Humanities and
  the School of Information\, the Technology Network of the Berkeley Econom
 y and Society Initiative (BESI)\; and the Berkeley Art\, Law\, and Finance
  Project\, hosted by the Berkeley Center for Law and Business at Berkeley 
 Law. In conjunction with the exhibition\, additional programming is develo
 ped in collaboration with Berkeley Art Museum and Pacific Film Archive (BA
 MPFA) and the Institute for Contemporary Art San Jose.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.berkeley.edu/live/events/324408-exhibition-hi
 dden-layers-ai-infrastructures-and-hallu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:berkeley:20260903T170000Z-323869@events.berkeley.edu
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260807T025549Z
DTSTART:20260903T170000Z
DTEND:20260903T180000Z
SUMMARY:OSPO All-Campus Virtual Meetup: September
LOCATION:Zoom
DESCRIPTION:Join us in shaping the future of open source at UC Berkeley\, 
 building on its rich legacy of leadership in open source software developm
 ent! At our monthly live online discussion and knowledge exchanges\, we ca
 n harness the collective intelligence and creativity of our community to m
 eaningfully transform how research is conducted\, produced\, and dissemina
 ted. Visit (https://bids.berkeley.edu/programs-initiatives/open-source-pro
 gram-office-ospo)the OSPO page (https://bids.berkeley.edu/programs-initiat
 ives/open-source-program-office-ospo) for more OSPO info and events.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ucospo.net/events/
END:VEVENT
